. Install required packages
pip install fastapi uvicorn jinja2
2. Project structure
project/
│
├── main.py
└── templates/
    └── index.html
3. FastAPI code — main.py
from fastapi import FastAPI, Request
from fastapi.templating import Jinja2Templates

app = FastAPI()

templates = Jinja2Templates(directory="templates")

@app.get("/")
def home(request: Request):
    name = "Yogeshwaran"
    course = "Python"

    return templates.TemplateResponse(
        "index.html",
        {
            "request": request,
            "name": name,
            "course": course
        }
    )
4. Jinja2 template — templates/index.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Dynamic Page</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Welcome, {{ name }}!</h1>

    <p>You are learning {{ course }}.</p>

</body>
</html>
How it works
Jinja2Templates connects FastAPI with Jinja2.
TemplateResponse() loads the HTML template.
{{ name }} and {{ course }} are Jinja2 variables.
FastAPI sends Python values to the HTML template.
Jinja2 replaces the variables with their actual values.

Run the application:

uvicorn main:app --reload

Then open:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/

Output:

Welcome, Yogeshwaran!

You are learning Python.
